{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"df8d7ec78670a51d","type":"group","x":460,"y":-240,"width":1120,"height":740,"label":"Diamond Model - Characterisation of an Exploit"},
		{"id":"c85764c76b248584","type":"group","x":-600,"y":-240,"width":960,"height":700,"label":"Diamond Model"},
		{"id":"3059bc034ca75df5","type":"group","x":-600,"y":-720,"width":1560,"height":400,"label":"Information"},
		{"id":"f9f6946aaa25ea36","type":"text","text":"## Core Features of Intrusion Event\n- **Adversary** - These are the parties responsible for the intrusion\n- **Capability** - This is a tool or technique that the adversary uses to attack the victim\n- **Infrastructure** - This is the network path or paths that the adversaries use to establish and maintain command and control over their capabilities\n- **Victim** - This is the target of the attack. However, a victim might be the target initially then later used as infrastructure to launch other attacks\n\nThe **adversary** uses **capability** over infrastructure to attack the **victim**","x":-240,"y":-700,"width":580,"height":360},
		{"id":"91baff89a99647af","type":"text","text":"## Meta Features\n(These features expand the model to include important elements)\n- **Timestamp** - Indicates the start and stop time of an event\n- **Phase** - Phase of the Cyber Kill Chain\n- **Result** - What was gained\n- **Direction** - Direction of the event across the Diamond model\n- **Methodology** - Used to classify the general type of event\n- **Resources** - External resources used by the adversary","x":400,"y":-675,"width":540,"height":310},
		{"id":"22e374709ba3d1ef","type":"text","text":"**Event** -> Time-bound activity that is restricted to a specific step in which an adversary uses a capability over infrastructure to attack a victim","x":-580,"y":-610,"width":293,"height":180},
